# RELAY: /home/tunnel/.ssh/authorized_keys  (chmod 600, owned by the tunnel user)
#
# Verified on OpenSSH 9.7 that each restriction below actually bites:
#   - command execution  -> "This account is not available"
#   - PTY                -> "PTY allocation request failed on channel 0"
#   - -L local forward   -> connection reset (permitopen mismatch)
#   - any other -R port  -> "remote port forwarding failed for listen port 13333"
#
# ⚠️ permitopen="none" is NOT valid in authorized_keys (only in sshd_config). An unparseable
#    option makes sshd reject the whole key, which presents as a bare "Permission denied
#    (publickey)" and wastes an afternoon. Pin -L to a dead target instead.
# ⚠️ permitlisten must match the bind address the client actually requests, so the client must
#    use -R 127.0.0.1:12222:... and not -R 12222:...
restrict,port-forwarding,permitlisten="127.0.0.1:12222",permitopen="127.0.0.1:1",command="/bin/false" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...REPLACE... buendia-pilot-tunnel
